From michal at ellpspace.math.ualberta.ca  Thu May  5 23:27:09 2005
From: michal at ellpspace.math.ualberta.ca (Michal Jaegermann)
Date: Thu, 5 May 2005 17:27:09 -0600
Subject: Fedora Core text install
In-Reply-To: <200505060014.18664.pgroen@osdev.xs4all.nl>;
	from pgroen@osdev.xs4all.nl on Fri, May 06, 2005 at 12:14:18AM
	+0200
References: <200505060014.18664.pgroen@osdev.xs4all.nl>
Message-ID: <20050505172709.A15473@ellpspace.math.ualberta.ca>

On Fri, May 06, 2005 at 12:14:18AM +0200, Peter M. Groen wrote:
> 
> Is there a way to do a text based install of Alpha Core 0.9?

Boot with '-fl i', list at aboot prompt (which will show up) what
predefined boot commands are available, and pick up by number that one
which has "text" string in its text.

Not that you cannot type a full boot command on your own.  Sometimes
this is useful.

   Michal



From rezso at rdsor.ro  Sun May  8 19:48:47 2005
From: rezso at rdsor.ro (Balint Cristian)
Date: Sun, 8 May 2005 22:48:47 +0300
Subject: AlphaCore 1.0 final release !
Message-ID: <200505082248.47885.rezso@rdsor.ro>

Salut !

	Proud to announce that me and Sergey, after a long hobby'sh development, finaly released Alpha Core 1.0 aka "Svetlana" !

   Svetlana is based on Fedora Core 3 release, it is a pure recompilation over alpha of fedora project with additional pain to fix platform specific
things to make it work. It olso already include latest fedora 3 updates.

In short line, iso's can be grabbed from [4xCD]:
	ftp://ftp.rdsor.ro/pub/Linux/Distributions/AlphaLinux/core/1.0/iso

The MD5SUM list:

073e9c4f1173bfefb9b2c21a34dbde96  svetlana-disk1.iso
5e7082d364f850706c281ec9ee17077b  svetlana-disk2.iso
50161c70f12fff7ca084f1d043242dd4  svetlana-disk3.iso
d8b755a1330dfd77bb8e962595076bbe  svetlana-disk4.iso


The main 1.0 yum-'ed repos can be found in this path:
	ftp://ftp.rdsor.ro/pub/Linux/Distributions/AlphaLinux/core/1.0/alpha
The yum.conf for the online tree  can be found:
ftp://ftp.rdsor.ro/pub/Linux/Distributions/AlphaLinux/core/yum.conf-1.0

	The old 1.0a tree was renumbered as 1.0 so you have to update you yum paths.

	One of milestone we attained is that unlike in ac-0.9 glibc was fixed properly so applications will run much more fine,
the kernel is olso much carefully assambled and tested on various machine, and the install disc contains the milo flavour too
for those who's machine require it. We strongly based on released test iso's as feedbacks wich was a very positive
surprise of successfull reactions, thanks again to axp-list members who tested it !

	After the install, the yum tool will contain the necessary paths to update tree so we will maintain
an update repository for this release. Olso i plan a extras tree for this release where fedora-extras packs
will be pushed.

	Becouse leak of more deep tests in real world, we reserves the fact that if a trivial bug is discovered by
anyone in the CD set we will try to rerelease this distro.


	As "hall of fame" want to thanks again to Jay from HP/Compaq for providing us lists of machine reports 
and for its time for us. Thanks Jay !
	Olso thanks for every happy alpha owners out there on the list !


	As last words, we hope for an alphacore-2.0 release too, it will be based on FC4, we try to put efforts to align this project
to fedora itself so all patches is moved right now into fedora mainline tree. Sergey is working to get gcc-4 and the build toolchain
to work proper on alpha and i dream some native java stuff in future alphacores like eg: eclipse and tomcat.

	For those who want to test even now the development tree we provide a yum config file:
ftp://ftp.rdsor.ro/pub/Linux/Distributions/AlphaLinux/core/yum.conf-devel



Happy installs for everyone !

 
~cristian

And again excuse me for any misstypes or horror lines, 
as latin native language writer.



