From mike at grouse.net.au  Tue May 10 15:23:52 2005
From: mike at grouse.net.au (Mike Barnes)
Date: Wed, 11 May 2005 01:23:52 +1000
Subject: Shameless Plug
Message-ID: <11DC3897-F12B-4469-879B-10B2FE1B9508@grouse.net.au>

I've finally got my act together and put up a live site for a project  
I've had in the back of my mind since 2001.

http://practicalunix.com/

I figured, while I was doing over the Alpha Core site, I'd throw the  
same combination of software together for this one too.

I've always wanted a forum for Unix-ish questions that had, as its  
primary goal, a complete lack of elitism. I know that there are some  
really clued-in people on this list, and I'd love to see some of the  
kind of attitudes this group has exhibited over the years I've been  
reading it take root there.

The site's motto is: "There Are No Stupid Questions", and I'm going  
to see that this is kept to, with my iron fist at the ready.

Of course, anyone trying to get things done using any Alpha running  
any Unix related operating system is welcome to stop by for attempts  
at help. Help regarding Alpha Core itself is still best directed to  
the http://alphacore.info/ site, but once you're up and running and  
want to configure Apache or make Samba do something odd, we'd be glad  
to lend a hand.



