Message-ID: <4287FECC.90500@sysmatrix.net>

Thanks to all who responded!!

It turns out that sector 1 and 2 need to be available but not partitioned. 

I was able to do this in Disk Druid by NOT selecting "new".  Instead I 
double clicked the free space and created a partition using sectors 1 
and 2.  I then created the rest of my partitions.  Finally as a last 
step I deleted the partition that used sectors 1 and 2.  This allowed 
boot loader to be installed on sectors 1 and 2.

Thanks again!

Jim

