I see them as well; in my very limited testing, they appear only a
couple of times during initial boot, and not once things settle down,
so I've attributed them to some bad behavior in PCI probing routines
that have been modified recently.

If they don't seem to happen once the system is up, it should be
possible to ignore them until something more drastic occurs, as we
in AlphaLinux land have done for years... ;-}

