ftp://alphalinux.rdsor.ro/pub/Linux/Distributions/AlphaLinux/core/1.0/SRPMS/kernel-2.6.11-1.1180axp_FC3.src.rpm

There are other modified source packages there.

>I also tried compiling vanilla 2.4.9 and 2.4.11.11 from kernel.org.  They compile ok (there was a gcc/ld internal error at one place during the compile (make boot), if I continued make from that point on, the build finished fine), but I have not been able to boot any of these -- I get a "cannot open initial console" and then the system hangs.
>  
>
You have to compile your kernel with initrd support and create initital 
ramdisk using mkinitrd. The FC3 uses only "udev" to manage /dev entries. 
mkinitrd will put necessary "udev" files to initial ramdisk. You will 
have to add "initrd=" option to your boot command. For more information 
please refer to home page to "udev".

Regards,

